  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (RNA-only, PCA, single-profile at 48.5% accuracy), the most critical uncertainty is whether the image modality provides any discriminative signal at all. This question gates a large portion of the search space (36 of 51 configs are multimodal). Config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is the cleanest possible test: it mirrors the structure of the RNA-only baseline (single profile, standard pretrained encoder) while swapping only the modality. If image accuracy substantially exceeds or falls below the RNA baseline, it immediately informs whether multimodal fusion is worth pursuing and which modality should anchor the best configuration. With 8 experiments remaining, resolving this fundamental modality question early is the highest-value use of the next slot, as it will guide whether to invest remaining budget in multimodal fusion, stronger RNA encoders, or image encoder upgrades."
}

